<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{"@type": "WebSite", "@id": "https://manalab.es/#website", "name": "ManaLab", "url": "https://manalab.es/", "inLanguage": ["en", "es"], "publisher": {"@id": "https://manalab.es/#org"}}, {"@type": "Organization", "@id": "https://manalab.es/#org", "name": "ManaLab", "url": "https://manalab.es/", "logo": {"@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://manalab.es/img/icono-192.png", "width": 192, "height": 192}, "sameAs": ["https://x.com/ManaLabApp", "https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab"]}, {"@type": "SoftwareApplication", "name": "ManaLab", "url": "https://manalab.es/", "description": "Free tracker for MTG Arena and Magic Online: opening hands and mulligans with screenshots, win rates by matchup, opponent deck, coach tools.", "applicationCategory": "GameApplication", "operatingSystem": "Windows 10, Windows 11", "softwareVersion": "2.3.2", "downloadUrl": "https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/latest", "image": "https://manalab.es/img/og.jpg", "screenshot": ["https://manalab.es/img/v22_repeticion.jpg", "https://manalab.es/img/en_panel.jpg", "https://manalab.es/img/en_partida.jpg", "https://manalab.es/img/en_estadisticas.jpg"], "inLanguage": ["en", "es", "fr", "de", "it", "pt-BR", "ja", "ko", "zh"], "offers": {"@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "EUR"}, "@id": "https://manalab.es/#app", "isPartOf": {"@id": "https://manalab.es/#website"}, "publisher": {"@id": "https://manalab.es/#org"}, "mainEntityOfPage": "https://manalab.es/", "applicationSubCategory": "MTG Arena and Magic Online match tracker"}, {"@type": "FAQPage", "inLanguage": "en", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Does it touch the game or give me an advantage in a match?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No, neither in Arena nor in Magic Online. It only reads the files the games write on your PC (Arena's Player.log; Magic Online's mtgo.log, Match_GameLog_*.dat, mtgo_game_history and grouping *.xml deck files), without modifying them. It doesn't modify Arena or Magic Online, doesn't read their memory and doesn't connect to their servers. The optional overlay is a separate window that only shows public information or what can be worked out from what has been played, never hidden information."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What data does it send?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Your games, screenshots and statistics stay in a folder on your PC. The program only downloads the updated meta deck lists, one per format (every 3 days), looks up card names on Scryfall (also with Magic Online ids) when it needs them, and asks GitHub once a day whether there's a new version. You can turn all three off in Settings. It sends data out only when you ask for something. The AI analysis sends that game's data (result, deck, hands, cards seen and timeline), never your name or the opponent's. A bug report sends what you write, your email if you add one, the ManaLab version, your system and language, whether you use Arena or Magic Online, an anonymous ID of your PC and, if you tick it, the last lines of registro.log with your user name and codes removed. It sends no games or decks."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Windows says «Windows protected your PC». Is it safe?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "That warning appears for programs without a paid code-signing certificate, which is common for small free tools. Click «More info» and then «Run anyway». It only shows on the first download: new versions install with «Update now» from inside the app, with no warning. To avoid it the first time too, before unzipping right-click the ZIP › Properties › tick «Unblock» › OK. Every version is checked on VirusTotal before it's published."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does it work with Magic Online?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, from 2.3. ManaLab records your Magic Online (MTGO) games: hands, mulligans, play or draw, the opponent's deck, statistics, replay and overlay. There is nothing to set up: it starts by itself when you open Magic Online, and you can import an mtgo.log file. What is different: Magic Online doesn't send turn phases or tapped cards, so ManaLab works them out from the log, and in the replay anything worked out is marked ≈ because it may not be exact. Magic Online doesn't give your sideboarded list in time either: ManaLab asks you to confirm your changes between games with one click, and until you do the overlay shows the list as unconfirmed. The overlay can show less than in Arena when the log has no table state. Your deck takes the name you saved it with in Magic Online when the list matches exactly; otherwise it is named by its colors."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does it work on Mac or Linux?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "For now it's for Windows 10 and 11. There is no native Linux version, and it has not been tested with Wine or Proton, so we can't promise it will work."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does it log Draft and Sealed (Limited)?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. It logs any Arena or Magic Online game, including Limited. The opponent's deck is compared with the meta decks of the game's format (Standard, Pioneer, Modern, Legacy, Vintage and Pauper); if nothing clearly matches, as in Limited, it is named by its colors."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is it free?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The program is free and needs no account. The only paid part is the AI loss analysis: 5 € per month, which pays for the AI service it uses. Every other feature is free."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I get the AI analysis?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Subscribe on Ko-fi (5 € per month). After paying you receive a subscription code by email. Paste it in Settings › Team and AI and the analysis appears in each lost game's Analysis tab. Want to try it first? Ask for a free trial by email."}}]}]}</script>
