<section class="seccion franja" id="coaches">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec">
<div class="eti">For coaches</div>
<h2>Study your games and work with your coach</h2>
</div>
<div class="novedades dos">
<div class="novedad">
<div class="ventana estrecha"><picture><source srcset="img/v22_informe_sesion.webp" type="image/webp"><img alt="The «Session report» dialog in ManaLab, where you pick options for a single file with the chosen games" height="672" loading="lazy" src="img/v22_informe_sesion.jpg" width="584"/></picture></div>
<div><div class="eti">Session report</div>
<h3>A session report for your coach</h3>
<p>Press «Prepare session» and pick the games: you get one file with hands, key moments and notes, to review or send to your coach.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="novedad">
<div class="ventana"><picture><source srcset="img/v22_tendencias.webp" type="image/webp"><img alt="ManaLab Statistics table of the most repeated mistakes with percentage of games and trend over the last 30 days" height="432" loading="lazy" src="img/v22_tendencias.jpg" width="1004"/></picture></div>
<div><div class="eti">Tags and trends</div>
<h3>Coach tags and trends</h3>
<p>Your coach tags mistakes per game or per step, and «What repeats the most» shows how each one evolves over 30 or 90 days, or your whole history.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
<p class="pie-captura">Screenshots with sample data from Arena.</p>
<p class="enlace-seccion"><a class="enlace-man" href="/coaches/">Guide for coaches: how to review a student →</a></p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion" id="empezar">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec" id="descargar">
<div class="eti">Get started</div>
<h2>Three steps, just once</h2>
</div>
<div class="pasos">
<div class="paso"><h3>Download and open</h3>
<p>Windows 10 or 11. Unzip the file and open ManaLab.exe. Nothing to install.</p>
<p style="margin-top:14px"><a class="boton prim" href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/download/v2.3.2/ManaLab-2.3.2-portable.zip" download data-descarga data-goatcounter-click="descarga" data-goatcounter-title="descarga-portada-en" id="enlace-descarga" rel="noopener"><span>Download free</span></a></p>
<p class="nota-descarga">Version <span data-version>2.3.2</span> · ZIP · <a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases" rel="noopener">other versions</a></p>
<template id="bloque-movil"><div class="movil-caja">
<h4 class="movil-tit">ManaLab runs on your computer</h4>
<p class="movil-txt">Send yourself the link and download it there.</p>
<p><button class="boton prim" data-compartir data-copiado="Link copied" data-titulo="compartir-movil-en" data-url="https://manalab.es/" type="button"><span>Send me the link</span></button></p>
<p class="movil-zip"><a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/download/v2.3.2/ManaLab-2.3.2-portable.zip" download data-descarga data-titulo="descarga-movil-en" rel="noopener">Download the ZIP anyway</a></p>
<p aria-live="polite" class="movil-estado" role="status"></p>
</div></template>
<p class="nota-smartscreen destacado" data-solo-pc>Before unzipping, right-click the ZIP › Properties › tick <b>Unblock</b> › OK: that way Windows neither shows «Windows protected your PC» nor blocks the program's files. If the warning still appears, click <b>More info › Run anyway</b>.</p>
<details data-solo-pc><summary>Already have ManaLab?</summary>
<p>Only needed on this first download: later versions install from inside the app with no warning.</p>
<p>Already on 2.1.0, 2.1.1 or 2.1.2? Update by hand one last time: unblock the ZIP as described above and unzip it over your ManaLab folder (your games and settings are kept). Those versions could open and close without showing the window; from 2.2 on, new versions install from inside the app.</p>
<p><a href="/safety/">Is it safe? Check it yourself →</a></p></details></div>
<div class="paso"><h3>Get your game ready</h3>
<p><b>Arena:</b> turn on <span class="ruta">Options › Account › Detailed Logs</span>. Without it, Arena doesn't write the games. <a href="/detailed-logs/">How to turn it on, step by step →</a></p>
<p style="margin-top:10px"><b>Magic Online:</b> nothing to set up. Open Magic Online and ManaLab picks it up on its own. The log path is in <span class="ruta">Settings › Games</span>, left on Default.</p></div>
<div class="paso"><h3>Play and review</h3>
<p><b>Press «Start logging».</b> Open ManaLab before playing and leave it running. Each match appears on the Dashboard when it ends.</p>
<p>Play Arena or Magic Online in windowed or borderless mode and review your games in Games. The app is free.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion franja" id="preguntas">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cab-sec"><div class="eti">FAQ</div><h2>Before you start</h2></div>
<div class="preguntas">
<details><summary>Does it touch the game or give me an advantage in a match?</summary>
<p>No, neither in Arena nor in Magic Online. It only reads the files the games write on your PC (Arena's Player.log; Magic Online's mtgo.log, Match_GameLog_*.dat, mtgo_game_history and grouping *.xml deck files), without modifying them. It doesn't modify Arena or Magic Online, doesn't read their memory and doesn't connect to their servers. The optional overlay is a separate window that only shows public information or what can be worked out from what has been played, never hidden information.</p></details>
<details><summary>What data does it send?</summary>
<p>Your games, screenshots and statistics stay in a folder on your PC. The program only downloads the updated meta deck lists, one per format (every 3 days), looks up card names on Scryfall (also with Magic Online ids) when it needs them, and asks GitHub once a day whether there's a new version. You can turn all three off in Settings. It sends data out only when you ask for something. The AI analysis sends that game's data (result, deck, hands, cards seen and timeline), never your name or the opponent's. A bug report sends what you write, your email if you add one, the ManaLab version, your system and language, whether you use Arena or Magic Online, an anonymous ID of your PC and, if you tick it, the last lines of registro.log with your user name and codes removed. It sends no games or decks.</p>
<p>More details: <a href="/safety/">Is ManaLab safe?</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Windows says «Windows protected your PC». Is it safe?</summary>
<p>That warning appears for programs without a paid code-signing certificate, which is common for small free tools. Click «More info» and then «Run anyway». It only shows on the first download: new versions install with «Update now» from inside the app, with no warning. To avoid it the first time too, before unzipping right-click the ZIP › Properties › tick «Unblock» › OK. Every version is checked on VirusTotal before it's published.</p>
<p>More details: <a href="/safety/">Is ManaLab safe?</a></p></details>
<details id="magic-online"><summary>Does it work with Magic Online?</summary>
<p>Yes, from 2.3. ManaLab records your Magic Online (MTGO) games: hands, mulligans, play or draw, the opponent's deck, statistics, replay and overlay. There is nothing to set up: it starts by itself when you open Magic Online, and you can import an mtgo.log file. What is different: Magic Online doesn't send turn phases or tapped cards, so ManaLab works them out from the log, and in the replay anything worked out is marked ≈ because it may not be exact. Magic Online doesn't give your sideboarded list in time either: ManaLab asks you to confirm your changes between games with one click, and until you do the overlay shows the list as unconfirmed. The overlay can show less than in Arena when the log has no table state. Your deck takes the name you saved it with in Magic Online when the list matches exactly; otherwise it is named by its colors.</p>
<p>On the website: <a href="/magic-online/">Magic Online tracker: what it saves and how it works</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Does it work on Mac or Linux?</summary>
<p>For now it's for Windows 10 and 11. There is no native Linux version, and it has not been tested with Wine or Proton, so we can't promise it will work.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does it log Draft and Sealed (Limited)?</summary>
<p>Yes. It logs any Arena or Magic Online game, including Limited. The opponent's deck is compared with the meta decks of the game's format (Standard, Pioneer, Modern, Legacy, Vintage and Pauper); if nothing clearly matches, as in Limited, it is named by its colors.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is it free?</summary>
<p>The program is free and needs no account. The only paid part is the AI loss analysis: 5 € per month, which pays for the AI service it uses. Every other feature is free.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I get the AI analysis?</summary>
<p>Subscribe on Ko-fi (5 € per month). After paying you receive a subscription code by email. Paste it in Settings › Team and AI and the analysis appears in each lost game's Analysis tab. Want to try it first? Ask for a free trial by <a href="mailto:manalab.app@gmail.com">email</a>.</p></details>
</div>
</div>
</section>
